# Process-level settings for `make run`. Copy to .env and edit; .env is gitignored.
#
# These are the knobs that describe HOW the server runs. Anything that describes how the
# LEAGUE runs — the pick clock, the keeper cost floor, roster shape, gates — belongs in
# data/strategy.yaml, which is read at boot. One source of truth per kind of thing.
#
#   draft.seconds_per_pick   the pick clock          -> data/strategy.yaml
#   keeper.cost_floor_round  round 8 keeper floor    -> data/strategy.yaml
#   roster.*, gates.*        league rules            -> data/strategy.yaml
#
# Changing either kind is a restart, never a rebuild.

PORT=8090
DATA=./data
TEAM=Sittin Purdy
